Parity notes:
  * Faithful SwiftUI port of the web pure-presentational first-run wizard. The web source has NO fetch,
    NO React-Query cache, NO Promise — it is gated only by a localStorage flag, a 1.5s setTimeout reveal,
    a cross-tab broadcast, and a local step index. Per the blessed pure-presentational precedent already
    established in this codebase by 22 sibling surfaces (Accordion 0203, InlineCallout 0124, MetricCard
    0095, StaggerItem 0194, ...), this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL states and does NOT
    fabricate loading/error/stale/offline chrome the source does not have. REAL states reproduced:
    hidden (already onboarded / before the timed reveal -> web `if (!visible) return null`), the four
    presented steps, the first/middle "Next" vs the final "Get Started" primary action, the progress
    indicators, dismissal (Skip / close / Escape / backdrop -> persist + broadcast), plus a calm
    completion leaf for the degenerate empty-catalog case (native "never a blank box").
  * Data bound via the shared P1/S8 state-holder layer (OnboardingWizardModel over an
    OnboardingWizardSource); no direct HTTP/storage/timer in the view.
  * Every string resolves through the P1/S10 facade (OnboardingWizardStrings); web copy verbatim; no
    English literals in Swift.
  * Tokens via P1/S9 (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSMotion); the web per-step hex maps
    to themeable brand tokens (accent / statusSuccess / statusWarning / chartSeriesPower).
  * Telemetry: emits view.opened with slug "OnboardingWizard" once, on the real present (P1/S11).
  * Accessibility: VoiceOver modal label + spoken step position + combined title/description, Dynamic
    Type, Reduce-Motion honoured at the reveal + step boundaries, Escape (.cancelAction) to dismiss.

